Consider adding additional assertions to ensure the plan structure remains as expected.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-17386:17428,17437:17477,17486:17565,17574:17622,17631:17684,17693:17742,17751:17800,17809:17846,17855:17931,17940:17991,18000:18064,18084:18104,18109:18120,18132:18229,18238:18310,18319:18418,18427:18496-16840:16884,16889:16893","promptId":"#QGZHP","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LocalPhysicalPlanOptimizerTests.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":17386,"endPos":17428,"startLine":390,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":390,"endLineOffset":50,"length":43},{"pos":17437,"endPos":17477,"startLine":391,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":391,"endLineOffset":48,"length":41},{"pos":17486,"endPos":17565,"startLine":392,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":392,"endLineOffset":87,"length":80},{"pos":17574,"endPos":17622,"startLine":393,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":393,"endLineOffset":56,"length":49},{"pos":17631,"endPos":17684,"startLine":394,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":394,"endLineOffset":61,"length":54},{"pos":17693,"endPos":17742,"startLine":395,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":395,"endLineOffset":57,"length":50},{"pos":17751,"endPos":17800,"startLine":396,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":396,"endLineOffset":57,"length":50},{"pos":17809,"endPos":17846,"startLine":397,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":397,"endLineOffset":45,"length":38},{"pos":17855,"endPos":17931,"startLine":398,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":398,"endLineOffset":84,"length":77},{"pos":17940,"endPos":17991,"startLine":399,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":399,"endLineOffset":59,"length":52},{"pos":18000,"endPos":18064,"startLine":400,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":400,"endLineOffset":72,"length":65},{"pos":18084,"endPos":18104,"startLine":401,"startLineOffset":19,"endLine":401,"endLineOffset":39,"length":21},{"pos":18109,"endPos":18120,"startLine":401,"startLineOffset":44,"endLine":401,"endLineOffset":55,"length":12},{"pos":18132,"endPos":18229,"startLine":402,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":402,"endLineOffset":105,"length":98},{"pos":18238,"endPos":18310,"startLine":403,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":403,"endLineOffset":80,"length":73},{"pos":18319,"endPos":18418,"startLine":404,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":404,"endLineOffset":107,"length":100},{"pos":18427,"endPos":18496,"startLine":405,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":405,"endLineOffset":77,"length":70}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":16840,"endPos":16884,"startLine":380,"startLineOffset":19,"endLine":380,"endLineOffset":63,"length":45},{"pos":16889,"endPos":16893,"startLine":380,"startLineOffset":68,"endLine":380,"endLineOffset":72,"length":5}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":103,"line":103,"comment_lines":["[][103]"],"review_comment":["use field.fold() since the field can be an expression such as 1 + 1 and you want to return the surrogate before the rest of the optimizer rules kick in.","Would love to just fold, but folding here is not safe unless we check if this will fold to `null`, first. That would require duplicating logic from `FoldNull`, though, which I\u0027d prefer to avoid.\r\n\r\n(Our evaluators cannot deal with null literals in general, and folding here results in the following exception when running e.g. `count(to_double(null))`:\r\n```\r\nillegal data type [null]\r\norg.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException: illegal data type [null]\r\n\tat __randomizedtesting.SeedInfo.seed([DBCF40F13A40EC92:539B7F2B94BC816A]:0)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.CsvTests.stats.Asdf(stats.csv-spec:1708)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException.illegalDataType(EsqlIllegalArgumentException.java:43)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException.illegalDataType(EsqlIllegalArgumentException.java:39)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.convert.AbstractConvertFunction.evaluator(AbstractConvertFunction.java:65)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.convert.AbstractConvertFunction.toEvaluator(AbstractConvertFunction.java:105)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.evaluator.mapper.EvaluatorMapper.fold(EvaluatorMapper.java:48)\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.EsqlScalarFunction.fold(EsqlScalarFunction.java:30)\r\n```\r\n)","Consider the rare case of count(1+1) - there might be count(1+null). This can be moved to a separate issue though to not block this one.","It makes sense to add more tests to account for these cases where an expression is evaluated, esp. to `null`. I\u0027ll do that in another PR, as this one should be backported to 8.14 as soon as possible.\r\n\r\nThese cases are covered in this PR, it\u0027s just that they result in an extra eval+projection.\r\n\r\n```\r\n| STATS count(1+null)\r\n```\r\n\r\nbecomes something equivalent to\r\n\r\n```\r\n| STATS x \u003d count(*)\r\n| EVAL `count(1+null)` \u003d COALESCE(MV_COUNT(1+null), 0) * x\r\n| KEEP `count(1+null)`\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich after folding becomes a multiplication of `count(*)` with 0. If we wanted to, we could further optimize this case to avoid the `count(*)` as well.","Opened a PR with additional tests: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/107888"],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","id":37860,"created_at":"2024-04-22T07:12:26Z","original_position":42,"side":"RIGHT","position":42,"submitted_on_commit":"496a2448383e0316baf22f3f3605daee2061682f","diff_hunk":"@@ -87,4 +93,30 @@ public Nullability nullable() {\n     protected TypeResolution resolveType() {\n         return EsqlTypeResolutions.isExact(field(), sourceText(), DEFAULT);\n     }\n+\n+    @Override\n+    public Expression surrogate() {\n+        var s \u003d source();\n+        var field \u003d field();\n+\n+        if (field.foldable()) {\n+            if (field instanceof Literal l) {","submitted_line":103},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The logic for handling foldable expressions in `surrogate()` methods seems correct but could be simplified and made more consistent. For example, the `Count` class checks if the field is a `Literal` and not a list before proceeding, while `CountDistinct` directly uses `Coalesce`. Consider standardizing this behavior across similar methods.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java--5928:6219","promptId":"#NFBQ1","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5928,"endPos":6219,"startLine":124,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":132,"endLineOffset":5,"length":292}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java--3407:4400","promptId":"#0VTRR","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3407,"endPos":4400,"startLine":97,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":121,"endLineOffset":5,"length":994}]}]}]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":116,"line":116,"comment_lines":["[][116]"],"review_comment":["Elsewhere in the code we use the convention of Count(1) - let\u0027s apply that here as well.","Hm, I tried to look for other places where `Count(1)` is used, but couldn\u0027t verify this (for ESQL at least).\r\n\r\nParsing `count()` results in `new Count(source, \"*\", KEYWORD)`, we also use the same in `Sum.surrogate()` and the (currently disabled) `NormalizeAggregate` used to replace all `count(literal)` by `count(*)` as well.\r\n\r\nFor consistency, I\u0027d like to stick to `count(*)` here."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","id":37861,"created_at":"2024-04-22T07:13:53Z","original_position":55,"side":"RIGHT","position":55,"submitted_on_commit":"496a2448383e0316baf22f3f3605daee2061682f","diff_hunk":"@@ -87,4 +93,30 @@ public Nullability nullable() {\n     protected TypeResolution resolveType() {\n         return EsqlTypeResolutions.isExact(field(), sourceText(), DEFAULT);\n     }\n+\n+    @Override\n+    public Expression surrogate() {\n+        var s \u003d source();\n+        var field \u003d field();\n+\n+        if (field.foldable()) {\n+            if (field instanceof Literal l) {\n+                if (l.value() !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 (l.value() instanceof List\u003c?\u003e) \u003d\u003d false) {\n+                    // TODO: Normalize COUNT(*), COUNT(), COUNT(\"foobar\"), COUNT(1) as COUNT(*).\n+                    // Does not apply to COUNT([1,2,3])\n+                    // return new Count(s, new Literal(s, StringUtils.WILDCARD, DataTypes.KEYWORD));\n+                    return null;\n+                }\n+            }\n+\n+            // COUNT(const) is equivalent to MV_COUNT(const)*COUNT(*) if const is not null; otherwise COUNT(const) \u003d\u003d 0.\n+            return new Mul(\n+                s,\n+                new Coalesce(s, new MvCount(s, field), List.of(new Literal(s, 0, DataTypes.INTEGER))),\n+                new Count(s, new Literal(s, StringUtils.WILDCARD, DataTypes.KEYWORD))","submitted_line":116},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The logic for handling foldable expressions in `surrogate()` methods seems correct but could be simplified and made more consistent. For example, the `Count` class checks if the field is a `Literal` and not a list before proceeding, while `CountDistinct` directly uses `Coalesce`. Consider standardizing this behavior across similar methods.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java--5928:6219","promptId":"#NFBQ1","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/CountDistinct.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":5928,"endPos":6219,"startLine":124,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":132,"endLineOffset":5,"length":292}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java--3407:4400","promptId":"#0VTRR","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Count.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3407,"endPos":4400,"startLine":97,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":121,"endLineOffset":5,"length":994}]}]}]}],"coveredGroundTruth":2,"uncoveredGroundTruth":0,"coveredMatchable":6,"uncoveredMatchable":12,"timing":76771,"tokensIn":13972,"tokensOut":577}